{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You conceive.</b> The tav is for the address to Assyria." "<b>חשש.</b> As it is in the language of Kedar, like מוץ." "<b>Your breath.</b> Some say: your breath shall be like fire, and it [f.gram.] shall consume you. But the correct view is that it is joined with חשש, and it is not a wind that shall carry you, but rather a fire that shall consume you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {2 "The bracketed note צ״ל היא indicates a correction in the Hebrew text: הוא (masc.) should read היא (fem.) to agree with the feminine אש. I rendered the corrected feminine form as 'it [f.gram.].'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:30.624580714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}